window.ATLAS.addDetails("earth.nodes",{"nodes":{
"earth-rotation-day-night":{"description":{"zh":"太阳光是平行光，任何时刻只照亮地球的一半；地球绕地轴自西向东自转，每个地方轮流转进亮面和暗面，转一圈就是一天；站在转动的地面上看，太阳就像从东边升起、西边落下。","en":"Sunlight arrives in parallel rays and lights only half the Earth at any moment; the Earth spins west to east on its axis, carrying every place through the bright half and the dark half in turn, one turn per day; seen from the turning ground, the Sun seems to rise in the east and set in the west."},"source":"../earth/astronomy/day-night-rotation/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"day-night-rotation","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"primary","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["为什么有白天和黑夜","地球自转","太阳为什么东升西落","晨昏线","自转和公转","一天为什么是 24 小时","昼夜交替","白天黑夜","为什么有白天黑夜","昼夜"],"en":["why is there day and night","Earth’s rotation","why does the sun rise in the east","terminator line","rotation and revolution","why is a day 24 hours","day and night cycle","day and night","why do we have day and night"]}},
"moon-phases":{"description":{"zh":"月亮永远亮半边；从地球看到的亮面比例是 (1 − cos θ)/2，周期约 29.5 天。假设圆轨道与平行光，北半球视角。","en":"The Moon is always half lit; the fraction seen from Earth is (1 − cos θ)/2 with a period of about 29.5 days. Assumes a circular orbit, parallel light and a northern-hemisphere view."},"formula":"f = (1 − cos θ) / 2","source":"../earth/astronomy/moon-phases/#step1","lessons":[{"slug":"moon-phases","step":1,"category":"earth","stage":"primary","primary":true}],"note":"group is earth & space; no atlas group exists for it","aliases":{"zh":["月亮为什么有圆缺","月有阴晴圆缺","月亮圆缺","上弦月 下弦月"],"en":["why does the moon change shape","phases of the moon","half moon","crescent moon"]}},
"contour-lines":{"description":{"zh":"等高线是同一海拔的点连成的线：相邻两条差一个等高距，越密坡越陡，水沿垂直于等高线的最陡方向往低处流。仅为虚构光滑地形的教学模型。","en":"Contour lines join points of equal altitude: neighbours differ by one contour interval, the closer they are the steeper the slope, and water runs downhill perpendicular to them. A teaching model on made-up smooth terrain."},"formula":"gap = Δh / slope","source":"../earth/geo/contour-lines/#step1","lessons":[{"slug":"contour-lines","step":1,"category":"earth","stage":"junior","primary":true}],"note":"No earth-science group in the atlas; group left OTHER. The edge to the existing 'derivative' node is a real link: slope from contour spacing is a rate of change."},
"latitude-longitude":{"description":{"zh":"纬度和经度是球面上的两个角度，合起来定位任意一点；纬线周长随 cos 纬度缩小，球面摊成平面必然变形，最短路是大圆弧，15° 经度对应 1 小时。仅为球形地球的教学模型。","en":"Latitude and longitude are two angles on a sphere that together locate any point; a parallel’s length shrinks with cos latitude, flattening a sphere necessarily distorts, the shortest route is a great-circle arc, and 15° of longitude is one hour. A teaching model of a spherical Earth."},"formula":"L(φ) = 2πR·cos φ","source":"../earth/geo/latitude-longitude/#step1","lessons":[{"slug":"latitude-longitude","step":1,"category":"earth","stage":"junior","primary":true}],"note":"No earth-science group in the atlas; group left OTHER. The edge to the existing 'unit-circle' node is a real link: a parallel's length scales with cos of latitude.","aliases":{"zh":["经纬度","经纬度是什么","经度","纬度"],"en":["latitude","longitude"]}},
"seasons-orbit":{"description":{"zh":"四季来自地轴倾斜约 23.4° 且方向不变，让太阳直射点一年内在南北回归线之间往返，正午太阳高度和昼长随之变化；日地距离只变化约 3%，不是原因。仅为几何模型，不含大气与热惯性。","en":"The seasons come from Earth’s axis being tilted about 23.4° in a fixed direction, so the overhead point swings between the tropics over a year and noon Sun height and day length follow; the Earth–Sun distance changes only about 3% and is not the cause. A geometric model without atmosphere or thermal lag."},"formula":"h = 90° − |φ − δ|","source":"../earth/astronomy/seasons-orbit/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"seasons-orbit","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"junior","primary":true}],"note":"No earth-science group in the atlas; group left OTHER. The edge to 'sine' is a real link: noon-altitude intensity is proportional to sin h.","aliases":{"zh":["为什么会有四季","四季是怎么来的","四季成因","夏天为什么热"],"en":["why do we have seasons","why are there seasons","what causes the seasons","why is summer hot"]}},
"atmospheric-circulation":{"description":{"zh":"赤道受热多、极地受热少推动空气环流，地球自转的科里奥利偏转把它拧成三圈与信风、西风带；陆海温差让季风随季节反向。理想化无大陆模型，数值为示意。","en":"More heating at the equator than the poles drives overturning, Coriolis deflection twists it into three cells with trade winds and westerlies, and land–sea contrast reverses monsoons with the season. An idealised model without continents; numbers are schematic."},"formula":"f = 2Ω sin φ","source":"../earth/climate/atmospheric-circulation/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"atmospheric-circulation","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"senior","primary":true}],"note":"No earth-science group in the atlas; group left OTHER. Edge sources are existing site pages (seasons-orbit, climate-energy) whose own fragments are merged separately."},
"carbon-cycle":{"description":{"zh":"用大气、陆地、表层海洋、深海与化石燃料五个碳库的账本，展示自然流量平衡、排放累积、碳的去向守恒，以及停排后下降缓慢。五库玩具模型，只显示趋势，不是预测。","en":"A five-reservoir ledger (air, land, surface ocean, deep ocean, fossil fuels) shows balanced natural flows, accumulating emissions, conservation of where the carbon goes, and the slow decline after emissions stop. A five-box toy model for trends, not a forecast."},"formula":"ΔA = E − uptake(land) − uptake(ocean)","source":"../earth/climate/carbon-cycle/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"carbon-cycle","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"senior","primary":true}],"note":"No earth-science group in the atlas; group left OTHER. Edges point to existing site pages (photosynthesis, climate-energy) merged separately."},
"climate-energy":{"description":{"zh":"阳光进来、红外出去，两边账要平：大气二氧化碳加厚，等于给出去的路加了道关卡，出少于进，地表就升温攒热量。气候问题本质是能量收支账，不是单日冷暖。","en":"Sunlight comes in, infrared goes out, and the two sides must balance: thicker atmospheric CO₂ puts a checkpoint on the way out, so out falls short of in and the surface warms as heat accumulates. Climate is an energy-budget ledger, not a single day's weather."},"source":"../earth/climate/climate-energy/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"climate-energy","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"senior","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["地球为什么变暖"],"en":["why is the planet warming"]}},
"climate-feedback":{"description":{"zh":"CO₂ 先让地球散热变难、带来一点初始升温；升温又让冰雪变少（反射的阳光减少）、空气里水汽变多（多吸红外），它们再推高温度——这些回路把一个小扰动放大，直到进出的能量重新平衡。","en":"CO₂ first makes it harder for the Earth to shed heat, causing some initial warming; that warming melts snow and ice (less sunlight reflected) and puts more water vapour in the air (more infrared absorbed), which push the temperature higher still — loops that amplify a small push until incoming and outgoing energy balance again."},"source":"../earth/climate/climate-feedback/#step2","lessons":[{"slug":"climate-feedback","step":2,"category":"earth","stage":"senior","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["气候反馈","冰雪反照率反馈","水汽反馈","正反馈","辐射强迫","全球变暖为什么会加速","气候临界点"],"en":["climate feedback","ice–albedo feedback","water vapour feedback","positive feedback","radiative forcing","why does global warming accelerate","climate tipping point"]}},
"plate-tectonics":{"description":{"zh":"地球的硬外壳碎成许多板块，漂在缓慢流动的软流圈上，每年只移动几厘米：相互分离处长出新地壳（洋中脊），相互汇聚处一块俯冲到另一块下面（海沟、火山、山脉），相互错动处应力积累、突然释放成地震。","en":"The Earth’s rigid shell is broken into plates riding on the slowly flowing asthenosphere, moving only a few centimetres a year: where they pull apart new crust forms (mid-ocean ridges), where they converge one dives beneath the other (trenches, volcanoes, mountains), and where they slide past each other stress builds and is released as earthquakes."},"source":"../earth/geo/plate-tectonics/#step1","lessons":[{"slug":"plate-tectonics","step":1,"category":"earth","stage":"senior","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["板块运动","大陆漂移","板块边界","洋中脊 海沟","为什么会地震","火山是怎么形成的","喜马拉雅山怎么来的","俯冲带","地震","地震是怎么发生的"],"en":["plate motion","continental drift","plate boundaries","mid-ocean ridge and trench","why do earthquakes happen","how are volcanoes formed","how did the Himalayas form","subduction zone","earthquake","earthquakes","what causes earthquakes"]}},
"cosmic-expansion":{"description":{"zh":"不是星系在静止的空间里从一个中心飞散，而是空间的刻度本身在拉开：所有星系间的距离按同一个尺度因子变大，所以越远的星系退行得越快（v = H₀d），它们发出的光在路上也被拉长成红移。","en":"Galaxies are not flying apart from a centre through still space; the ruler of space itself is stretching: every distance between galaxies grows by the same scale factor, so farther galaxies recede faster (v = H₀d), and their light is stretched into a redshift on the way."},"formula":"v = H₀d,  λ = (1+z)λ₀","source":"../earth/astronomy/cosmology-expansion/#step1","lessons":[{"slug":"cosmology-expansion","step":1,"category":"earth","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["宇宙膨胀","哈勃定律","哈勃常数","宇宙学红移","尺度因子","宇宙有中心吗","星系为什么在远离我们","大爆炸","宇宙大爆炸"],"en":["expanding universe","Hubble’s law","Hubble constant","cosmological redshift","scale factor","does the universe have a centre","why are galaxies moving away from us","Big Bang","big bang","the big bang","hubble's law"]}},
"kepler-orbits":{"description":{"zh":"行星沿椭圆绕恒星运行，恒星在一个焦点上；偏心率越大，椭圆越扁；离恒星近时跑得快、远时跑得慢（开普勒第二定律）；当轨道恰好侧对着我们，行星经过恒星前方会挡住一点星光，这就是凌日。","en":"A planet travels round its star on an ellipse with the star at one focus; the larger the eccentricity, the flatter the ellipse; it moves fast when close to the star and slowly when far (Kepler’s second law); when the orbit is seen edge-on, the planet passing in front of the star blocks a little of its light — a transit."},"source":"../earth/astronomy/kepler-orbits/","lessons":[{"slug":"kepler-orbits","step":null,"category":"earth","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["开普勒定律","椭圆轨道","开普勒第二定律","面积定律","偏心率","近日点 远日点","凌日法找系外行星","行星为什么离太阳近时更快","开普勒三定律","行星轨道"],"en":["Kepler’s laws","elliptical orbit","Kepler’s second law","law of equal areas","eccentricity","perihelion and aphelion","transit method for exoplanets","why do planets move faster near the sun","kepler's laws","planetary orbits"]}}
}});
